server: honour --file-watcher-polling again (the recursive watcher options were never passed)

The server's `--file-watcher-polling <interval>[:<path>...]` option makes the recursive file watcher poll instead of relying on change
notifications, for file systems that send none (network shares, FUSE, the virtiofs folders that a VM shares from its host).
RemoteAgentFileSystemProviderChannel's SessionFileWatcher reads the option in its override of getRecursiveWatcherOptions(), but
AbstractSessionFileWatcher never calls that method: it creates its DiskFileSystemProvider without options, so the recursive watch
requests never get a polling interval and the option has no effect. Edits made outside the machine that runs the server are then not
seen until something else touches the folder.

This passes the subclass's recursive watcher options to the provider, which is what the method exists for. Without the option the result
is undefined, the provider's default: nothing changes for a server started without --file-watcher-polling.

--- a/src/vs/platform/files/node/diskFileSystemProviderServer.ts
+++ b/src/vs/platform/files/node/diskFileSystemProviderServer.ts
@@ -289,7 +289,7 @@
 	) {
 		super();

-		this.fileWatcher = this._register(new DiskFileSystemProvider(logService));
+		this.fileWatcher = this._register(new DiskFileSystemProvider(logService, { watcher: { recursive: this.getRecursiveWatcherOptions(environmentService) } }));

 		this.registerListeners(sessionEmitter);
 	}
